Last week at a wedding dinner, the host asked me to sit next to Mr Green.
Mr Green was a thin, serious man in a dark grey suit.
He did not even smile when I took my seat beside him.
His eyes were fixed on his soup and in a short time, he was busy eating.
I tried to make conversation.
‘A new film is showing at “The Odeon” this week,’ I said.
‘Will you be seeing it?’ ‘No,’ he answered.
‘Will you be travelling anywhere this summer?’ I asked. ‘No,’ he answered.
‘Will you be staying in London?’ I asked. ‘No,’ he answered.
In despair, I asked him whether he liked the food.
‘Young man,’ he said, ‘if you talked less and ate more, we would both have a better time!’